      <activity id="25746f64-931b-5d8f-a4ee-306b806c02b2" activityNameId="b2977ce7-902f-5898-a170-2c2ace4fba2c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Methylene diphenyl diisocyanate, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Methylene diphenyl diisocyanate, at plant
Data are from the Eco-profiles of the European plastics industry (PlasticsEurope). Not included are the values reported for: recyclable wastes, amount of air / N2 / O2 consumed, unspecified metal emission to air and to water, mercaptan emission to air, unspecified CFC/HCFC emission to air, dioxin to water. The amount of "sulphur (bonded)" is assumed to be included into the amount of raw oil.;
CAS number: 000101-68-8; 
UUID: c35b697b-e4d0-3d3b-874f-8e1554a6ad67
Aggregated data for all processes from raw material extraction until delivery at plant
Location: 5 European production sites (B,D,I, NL)
Technology: production out of phosgene, aniline and formaldehyde
Time period: time to which data refer
Production volume: 560 kt
Sampling: literature values based on company survey 
Extrapolations: no extrapolation
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_c35b697b-e4d0-3d3b-874f-8e1554a6ad67.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
